    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Total includes FERC account 922 (Adm. Expense Transferred - Cr). This account is not listed in the 18 CFR Part 367 Uniform System of Accounts for Centralized Service Companies, but is included in 18 CFR Part 101. While Entergy's service companies have adopted 18 CFR Part 367, Entergy generally records service company costs on the service companies' books using the same accounts recorded on the affiliates' books as a result of the service company billing. The amount recorded in account 922 was billed to affiliates based on allocation methods as filed with the FERC in Entergy's Rate Schedule 435, a form of service agreement for the provision of goods and services. Once billed to the affiliate companies, this amount is properly includable in account 922 per CFR Part 101.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
